<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37286" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏtentĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town in Picenum</i>, now <i>S. Maria
				di Potenza</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 39, 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Har.
				Resp. 28, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 13, 18, §
			111</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏtentīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Potentian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Colon. p. 123</span></i>
			 Goes.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town in Lucania</i>, now <i>Potenza;</i> hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏtentīni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Potentia</i>, <i>in Lucania</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 11, 15, § 98</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
